Heather Coppersmith, cunningly disguised as me@privacy.net wrote:

> When do you make a stash?  Right when you're burdened?  When you
> find "an appropriate place" (whatever that may be)?

Whenever I get burdened.

> Where do you make a stash?  In the nearest box or chest?  Near a
> particular dungeon feature?  How far do you drag a chest over to
> that appropriate place?

I drag any chest to the deepest altar in the known main dungeon. If I
haven't found an altar yet, I put that chest next to the downstairs into
the Gnomish Mines. If I've found Sokoban, I normally put my stash there,
on its deepest (first) level, without bothering with a chest.

After I've cleared the Mines and BUC-identified everything on its altar, I
drag everything except body armour up to the chest next to the Mines'
entrance. Yes, I mean everything. No item remains in the Mines.

I then make a second stash, somewhere deeper in the main dungeon, or on
the first level of Sokoban, and again move everything over there. My name
is Efembe, the prototypical packrat.

As soon as I find a better (deeper) place to make a stash, I do so, and
return to my previous stash to move everything out of there, leaving only
a few things like spare food items which I might need later and don't want
to travel too far for.

Moving a stash usually means a *lot* of trips up and down (even with a
blessed bag of holding, it usually takes me an hour of playing time, and
several thousands of NetHack turns). Some twenty trips up and down isn't
unusual for me.

> How do you make a stash?  I know that stacking a boulder on top of
> a box or a chest on top of the E-word is the best, although I
> haven't lost anything I've simply left in a big pile next to the
> stairs, either.

I usually use a chest or any other type of container. I don't bother with
a boulder on top of it. If a gelatinous cube reaches it, it will only
digest the box, but its contents will be unharmed.

As for the stash itself, I normally sort them inside, putting stackable
items in first, then non-stackable things. When stackable items didn't
merge yet (in 3.3.1, I believe), I even took out the old ones first, so
the would merge in my directory before I immediately put them back in
again.

> Do you make different kinds of stashes for different kinds of
> items?  A box of polypile fodder on one level and a box of water
> just begging to become holy on another?

Sometimes, when the contents of my box become unmanageable (lilke over
thirty pages of stuff), I resort to several boxes. I usually have one for
identified, useful stuff that I wish to hang on to, one for polypile
fodder, and one for yet-to-identify stuff (at first, these are "iron
wands" and the like, lateron, it's "wand of death"s with unknown charges
in this one).

If I'm playing polypileless, I replace that second one by a cursed bag of
holding, and take things in and out repeatedly to remove the unwanted
items from my game (makes for a smaller save file).

